<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Bzhedugh</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A princely Circassian tribe on the lower Kuban, one of the few Adyghe groups that largely remained in their homeland after 1864.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bzhedugh were one of the aristocratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Adyghe</a> tribes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/circassia">Circassia</a>, living along the left bank of the Kuban and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psekups">Psekups</a> river near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Krasnodar</a>. They are recorded as a distinct princely community by the 16th and 17th centuries; their earlier history is not recorded separately.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Princes and nobles held power over free peasants and serfs. When the commoners of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/shapsugs">Shapsugs</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natukhaj">Natukhaj</a> rebelled against their nobility, Bzhedugh princes backed the aristocrats and were defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bziyuqo">Bziyuqo</a> in 1796. The tribe lay close to Russian forts on the Kuban and often negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> while trading and fighting with it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Bzhedugh came under Russian control in the course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-circassian-war">Russo-Circassian War</a>, which the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> completed in 1864. More of them stayed than most Circassian groups, and they form a large part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Adyghe</a> population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adygea">Adygea</a> today.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1500 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.24%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1864 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Adyghe</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bzhedugh, Bzhedukh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=principality-of-bzhedugh" aria-label="Principality of Bzhedugh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5609 212 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Bzhedugh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5955 888h0M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5929 468h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5929 468h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=principality-of-bzhedugh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

